## You do not need this file, and an `apps/frontend/.env` beside it is NOT read.
##
## `svelte.config.js` pins `kit.env.dir` to the repo root, so the ONE env file this app
## reads is `<repo-root>/.env`. Use `<repo-root>/.env.example` as the template.
##
## This file used to say "you most likely don't need this unless you're running the front
## separately" — which was wrong in a way that cost a debug session. SvelteKit defaulted
## `kit.env.dir` to `process.cwd()` (= `apps/frontend`), so a stale local `apps/frontend/.env`
## was in fact the ONLY file being read, and the entire repo-root configuration was invisible.
## Bank auth silently fell back to the wrong identity provider and built an authorize URL with
## an empty `client_id` and no origin. See `.planning/debug/resolved/idura-bank-auth-empty-client.md`.
##
## If you have an `apps/frontend/.env` left over from before, it is now inert — delete it so it
## cannot mislead you into thinking a value is configured when the app never sees it.